1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,633
Let's have a look at a map of liverpool and you'll notice that everything is contained within this rectangle.
我们来看看利物浦的地图，你会发现导览中的地方都集中在这个长方形里。

2
00:00:05,633 --> 00:00:10,620
It's very easy to get around the city and everything is within walking distance.
他说，在市区走动很方便，这些地点都在步行可达的范围内。

3
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:17,460
Believe it or not you could see literally everything that liverpool has to offer by walking in a square.
信不信由你，他说沿着方形路线走，就能看到利物浦提供的几乎所有景点。

4
00:00:17,460 --> 00:00:23,169
And we'll start right here next to the water at a section of the city called pier head.
我们就从这里、水边这个叫 Pier Head 的市区片区开始。

5
00:00:23,169 --> 00:00:26,940
Where you'll find the three most important buildings in liverpool.
在这里，你会看到他所说的利物浦最重要的三座建筑。

6
00:00:28,380 --> 00:00:33,480
They are known as the three graces and they dominate the liverpool skyline.
它们被称为 Three Graces，也就是三美神建筑，构成了利物浦醒目的天际线。

7
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:43,129
But probably the most famous out of the three graces the royal liver building formerly home to the royal liver company.
其中最著名的，大概就是皇家利物大厦；它以前是皇家利物公司的所在地。

8
00:00:43,129 --> 00:00:52,440
It's the most famous building in all of liverpool and certainly it's most recognizable with its twin towers and its two liver birds guarding the top.
他说，这既是利物浦最著名的建筑，也肯定是最容易辨认的；它有双塔，顶部有两只利物鸟守望。

9
00:00:52,440 --> 00:00:55,244
This building can be seen from miles away.
几英里外就能看到这座楼。

10
00:00:55,244 --> 00:00:59,100
You can pay for a tour of the royal liver building.
你可以付费参加皇家利物大厦的参观导览。

11
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:03,660
Admittedly some of the history can be quite boring if you're not into that sort of thing.
他承认，如果你不喜欢这类内容，有些历史介绍可能会挺无聊。

12
00:01:04,320 --> 00:01:09,420
But the highlights of a tour of the royal liver building is actually getting to climb up the clock towers.
但他说，参观的一大亮点，是可以爬上钟塔。

13
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:12,300
Looking around the inside of the clock mechanisms.
还可以看看时钟机械装置的内部。

14
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:16,980
And you get these wonderful views of the city of liverpool from up here.
而且，从这里还能欣赏利物浦漂亮的城市景色。

15
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:20,210
The views themselves are probably worth the price of admission.
他觉得，光是这些景色，大概就值回门票了。

16
00:01:20,210 --> 00:01:26,160
Whilst we're up here actually let me tell you about the story of these two liver birds.
既然我们已经在上面了，我就给大家讲讲这两只利物鸟的故事。

17
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:29,258
The two liver birds guard the city of liverpool.
这两只利物鸟守望着利物浦这座城市。

18
00:01:29,258 --> 00:01:34,065
The male at the back over there known as bertie watches over the inhabitants.
他说，后面那只雄鸟叫 Bertie，守望着城里的居民。

19
00:01:34,065 --> 00:01:39,208
And the female looking out at sea known as bella looks after all the sailors.
而面朝大海的雌鸟叫 Bella，照看着所有水手。

20
00:01:39,208 --> 00:01:46,713
There's a superstition that states that if these two birds were to ever leave the city of liverpool will come crumbling down.
有一种迷信说，如果这两只鸟离开，利物浦就会轰然倒塌。

21
00:01:46,713 --> 00:01:51,266
So even though these birds are made of stone and can't move by themselves.
所以，尽管作者把鸟像描述为石头做的，自己又不会动……

22
00:01:51,266 --> 00:01:54,480
They literally chain them to the towers just in case.
他们还是给它们拴上链条，固定在塔楼上，以防万一。

23
00:01:55,140 --> 00:02:00,180
The second of the three graces is known as the cunard building.
三美神建筑中的第二座叫丘纳德大厦。

24
00:02:00,180 --> 00:02:06,796
Traditional headquarters of the famous cunard cruise liners is now home to the british music experience.
它曾是著名的丘纳德邮轮公司的总部，拍摄时这里设有 British Music Experience 音乐展馆。

25
00:02:06,796 --> 00:02:12,870
If you're a big fan of british music this interactive display would be actually quite good.
如果你很喜欢英国音乐，他觉得这个互动展览会很不错。

26
00:02:12,870 --> 00:02:18,300
It's got a lot of history musical artefacts you can sing and dance along if you want to.
里面有不少历史和音乐文物；想参与的话，还可以跟着唱歌跳舞。

27
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:23,820
And overall if you're a musician or somebody who's into music it's actually pretty good.
总的来说，如果你是音乐人，或者喜欢音乐的人，他觉得这里确实挺好。

28
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:29,592
The third of the three graces is the port of liverpool building.
三美神建筑中的第三座，是利物浦港务大厦。

29
00:02:29,592 --> 00:02:35,010
Traditionally this would have been the administrative centre for the entire port of liverpool.
过去，这里应当是整个利物浦港的行政管理中心。

30
00:02:35,010 --> 00:02:38,576
But nowadays I believe it's mainly offices and residences.
不过，他认为拍摄时它主要被用作办公室和住宅。

31
00:02:38,576 --> 00:02:43,932
But if you ask security nicely they'll actually let you into the ground floor.
他说，如果你礼貌地询问保安，他们会让你进入底层。

32
00:02:43,932 --> 00:02:47,580
Where you can experience some of the wonderful architecture of this building.
在那里，你能欣赏这座建筑精美的建筑设计。

33
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:55,380
Please note that this isn't actually a tourist attraction it is a working building and a working residence so please bear that in mind.
请注意，这其实不是旅游景点，而是仍在使用的办公与居住建筑，所以请记住这一点。

34
00:02:56,460 --> 00:03:01,836
So outside the three graces you'll find the famous statue of king edward vii.
那么，三美神建筑外面有一尊著名的爱德华七世雕像。

35
00:03:01,836 --> 00:03:06,420
It provides an amazing photo opportunity even with a seagull on his head.
这里是很棒的拍照地点，哪怕他的头上正停着一只海鸥。
